      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: route bindings return the wrong agent when route identifiers contain separators",
        "body": "Fixes an issue where route bindings can return the wrong agent when route cache key fields contain separator characters. The old cache key concatenated channel, account, peer, guild, team, and role fields with tab and comma delimiters. If any of those fields contained those same delimiters -- for example a peer named \"room-1-guild-2\" or role IDs containing commas -- two genuinely distinct routing contexts would share one cache key and the wrong cached route could be returned.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe cache key is now a JSON-serialized array. Array elements are individually encoded by JSON.stringify, so no field value can accidentally form a delimiter when concatenated. The three remaining hyphen sentinel fallbacks (`guildId || \"-\"`, `teamId || \"-\"`) are replaced with `?? null` -- null serializes as a distinct JSON literal, so an absent field and the literal string \"-\" produce different cache keys.\n\n## User Impact\n\nRouting contexts whose peer, guild, team, or role identifiers contain tab, comma, or hyphen characters no longer risk receiving the wrong agent through a cache collision. The binding evaluation order, matching logic, and fallback behavior are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Cache collision regression\n\nBefore fix (old `|| \"-\"` sentinels): an absent guildId and the literal string \"-\" produced the same cache key. The cached route for one returned the wrong agent for the other.\n\nAfter fix (`?? null` in JSON array): absent fields serialize as `null`, distinct from any string literal including \"-\". Different routing contexts produce different cache keys and resolve independently.\n\nNew regression test (57/57 passed): `does not reuse a cached route when guildId is omitted versus the literal hyphen string` -- exercises the exact collision scenario the old sentinel permitted.\n\n### Test coverage\n\n- `resolve-route.test.ts`: 57 tests pass (3 new: peer+guild separator collision, role comma collision, and hyphen-sentinel collision). All three fail against the old delimiter-concatenated cache key.\n- Scoped `oxfmt`, `oxlint`, and `git diff --check` pass.\n\nAI-assisted.\n",
